From: Jahshaka <jahshaka@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] HlmsDiskCache::copyFrom: skip a shader-cache entry that has no PSO instead of crashing

WHY (Jahshaka lane E2, 2026-09-12 — measured crash)

`Hlms::createShaderCacheEntry` pushes the HlmsCache entry before the backend
creates the PSO. When the compile FAILS — an uncompilable property combination,
a driver rejecting the generated source — the entry stays in `mShaderCache`
with a default-constructed `HlmsPso`: `macroblock` and `blendblock` are null.

`HlmsDiskCache::Pso`'s constructor dereferences both unconditionally
(`macroblock( *srcPsoCache->pso.macroblock )`), so SAVING the disk cache after
any failed compile is a SIGSEGV at address 0 inside
`HlmsDiskCache::Pso::Pso` / `HlmsDiskCache::copyFrom` — the process dies over a
shader that had merely failed to compile, which is a recoverable condition
everywhere else in the engine.

Measured: a PBS pixel shader generated against an inconsistent shadow-node
light count ("'hlms_shadowmap3' : undeclared identifier") left such an entry,
and the app's periodic shader-cache save crashed on the next tick.

THE FIX: skip an entry with no PSO and log it loudly (LML_CRITICAL names the
hash). The cache is still saved, without the entry that has nothing to save; a
compile failure degrades instead of killing the process.

diff --git a/OgreMain/src/OgreHlmsDiskCache.cpp b/OgreMain/src/OgreHlmsDiskCache.cpp
index 93ca8f9fe..2e9306339 100644
--- a/OgreMain/src/OgreHlmsDiskCache.cpp
+++ b/OgreMain/src/OgreHlmsDiskCache.cpp
@@ -189,6 +189,26 @@ namespace Ogre
                     }
                 }
 
+                // A SHADER THAT FAILED TO COMPILE LEAVES AN ENTRY WITH NO PSO
+                // (Jahshaka). Hlms::createShaderCacheEntry adds the cache entry
+                // before the backend builds the PSO, so when the compile throws
+                // (a bad property combination, a driver rejecting the source)
+                // the entry survives with a default-constructed HlmsPso whose
+                // macroblock and blendblock are null — and this copy
+                // dereferences both. Saving the disk cache then crashed the
+                // process over a shader that had merely failed: skip the entry
+                // and say so, once per cache copy.
+                if( bCacheable && ( !( *itor )->pso.macroblock || !( *itor )->pso.blendblock ) )
+                {
+                    bCacheable = false;
+                    LogManager::getSingleton().logMessage(
+                        "HlmsDiskCache: skipping shader cache entry " +
+                            StringConverter::toString( ( *itor )->hash ) +
+                            " - it has no PSO (its shader failed to compile). The disk cache will "
+                            "be saved without it.",
+                        LML_CRITICAL );
+                }
+
                 if( bCacheable )
                 {
                     Pso pso( hlms->mRenderableCache[renderableIdx], hlms->mPassCache[passIdx], *itor );
